      "text": "We denote unsafe regions of state space, or obstacles, as",
      "bbox": [
        321.9399108886719,
        94.84930419921875,
        563.0391235351562,
        103.75586700439453
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Xobs ⊂X. We assume obstacles are static but different in each",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        106.0870132446289,
        563.0355224609375,
        116.98670196533203
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "episode, as the focus of this work is not on predicting other",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        118.76031494140625,
        563.035400390625,
        127.66687774658203
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "agents’ motion. Furthermore, reachability-based frameworks",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        130.71533203125,
        563.035400390625,
        139.62188720703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "exist to handle other agents’ motion [33], [49], so the present",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        142.67034912109375,
        563.035400390625,
        151.576904296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "work can extend to dynamic environments.",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        154.6253662109375,
        488.4154357910156,
        163.53192138671875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We further assume the robot can instantaneously sense all",
      "bbox": [
        321.9399108886719,
        167.88037109375,
        563.03466796875,
        176.78692626953125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "obstacles (that is, Xobs) and represent them as a union of",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        179.11904907226562,
        563.032958984375,
        189.59136962890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "constrained zonotopes. In the case of sensing limits, one can",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        191.7913818359375,
        563.035400390625,
        200.69793701171875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "determine a minimum distance within which obstacles must",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        203.74639892578125,
        563.0353393554688,
        212.6529541015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "be detected to ensure safety, given a robot’s maximum speed",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        215.701416015625,
        563.035400390625,
        224.60797119140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and braking distance [32, Section 5].",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        227.65643310546875,
        463.3296203613281,
        236.56298828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "C. Reachable Sets",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        242.99407958984375,
        387.53424072265625,
        251.5818328857422
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We ensure safety by computing our robot’s forward reach-",
      "bbox": [
        321.9399108886719,
        259.1484375,
        563.0348510742188,
        268.05499267578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "able set (FRS) for a given motion plan, then adjusting the plan",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        271.10345458984375,
        563.035400390625,
        280.010009765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "so that the FRS lies outside of obstacles. We deﬁne the FRS,",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        283.0594482421875,
        563.0353393554688,
        291.96600341796875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "henceforth called the reachable set, as follows:",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        295.0144348144531,
        503.8973388671875,
        303.9209899902344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Deﬁnition 1. The reachable set Rk at time step k, subject",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779052734375,
        313.5301208496094,
        563.0327758789062,
        324.4188537597656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "to a sequence of inputs uj ∈Uj ⊂Rm, noise wj ∈W",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        324.50225830078125,
        561.647705078125,
        336.3837890625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "∀j ∈{0, . . . , k −1}, and initial set X0 ∈Rn, is the set",
      "bbox": [
        311.97796630859375,
        336.4572448730469,
        544.2081909179688,
        348.33978271484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Rk =",
      "bbox": [
        321.8089599609375,
        352.38409423828125,
        344.7928771972656,
        363.8417053222656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "\b",
      "bbox": [
        347.5579528808594,
        351.3875427246094,
        353.36614990234375,
        357.76361083984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "xk ∈Rn \f\f xj+1 = f(xj, uj) + wj, x0 ∈X0,",
      "bbox": [
        353.3699645996094,
        349.89306640625,
        539.5165405273438,
        363.8416748046875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "uj ∈Uj, and wj ∈W, ∀j = 0, · · · , k −1",
      "bbox": [
        353.36993408203125,
        367.4280700683594,
        533.01025390625,
        378.3267517089844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": ".",
      "bbox": [
        538.8219604492188,
        367.4280700683594,
        541.591552734375,
        377.39068603515625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(3)",
      "bbox": [
        551.4199829101562,
        360.67340087890625,
        563.0364379882812,
        369.5799560546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Recall that we treat the dynamics f as a black box (e.g., a",
      "bbox": [
        321.94000244140625,
        385.2110900878906,
        563.0333862304688,
        395.1737060546875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "simulator), which could be nonlinear and difﬁcult to model,",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        397.8833923339844,
        563.0355834960938,
        406.7899475097656
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "but we still seek to conservatively approximate (that is, over-",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        409.83837890625,
        563.0355834960938,
        418.74493408203125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "approximate) the reachable set Rk.",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        421.0760498046875,
        455.41168212890625,
        431.3959045410156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "D. Safe RL Problem Formulation",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        437.1310119628906,
        449.07330322265625,
        445.7187805175781
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We denote the state of the RL agent at time k by ˆxk ∈RnRL,",
      "bbox": [
        321.9400329589844,
        451.5851745605469,
        563.0366821289062,
        463.46771240234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "which contains the state xk of the robot plus information such",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        464.52301025390625,
        563.0408325195312,
        475.6418762207031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "as sensor measurements and previous actions. At each time k,",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        476.4779968261719,
        563.0366821289062,
        486.44061279296875
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the RL agent chooses uk. Recall that Xobs ⊂Rn denotes",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        485.5353088378906,
        563.0368041992188,
        499.3326721191406
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "obstacles. For a given task, we construct a reward function",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        501.1062927246094,
        563.0357055664062,
        510.0128479003906
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "ρ : (ˆxk, uk) 7→rk ∈R (examples of ρ are given in Section",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        512.2059936523438,
        563.03173828125,
        523.24267578125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "IV). At time k, let pk = (uj)nplan",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779968261719,
        521.425048828125,
        448.1457824707031,
        535.7565307617188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "j=k denote a plan, or sequence",
      "bbox": [
        434.6429748535156,
        525.0162353515625,
        563.0390625,
        536.9277954101562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of actions, of duration nplan ∈N.",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        536.2539672851562,
        446.7926940917969,
        547.1536254882812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Then, our safe RL problem is as follows. We seek to learn",
      "bbox": [
        321.9410400390625,
        550.227294921875,
        563.0360107421875,
        559.1338500976562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a policy πθ : ˆxk 7→uk, represented by a neural network with",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        561.3259887695312,
        563.0350952148438,
        572.9215698242188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "parameters θ, that maximizes expected cumulative reward.",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        573.4199829101562,
        563.035888671875,
        583.382568359375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Note that the policy can be deterministic or stochastic. Since",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        586.09228515625,
        563.035400390625,
        594.9988403320312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "rolling out the policy na¨ıvely may lead to collisions, we also",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        597.998291015625,
        563.0337524414062,
        606.9537963867188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "seek to create a safety layer between the policy and the robot",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        610.0032958984375,
        563.0357055664062,
        618.9098510742188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(that is, to ensure Rj ∩Xobs = ∅for all j ≥k).",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        621.240966796875,
        507.9151611328125,
        632.6975708007812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "III. BLACK-BOX REACHABILITY-BASED SAFETY LAYER",
      "bbox": [
        317.906982421875,
        638.2022705078125,
        557.1132202148438,
        647.1088256835938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "We unite three components into our BRSL system for",
      "bbox": [
        321.9410095214844,
        655.4422607421875,
        563.0359497070312,
        664.3488159179688
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "collision-free motion planning without a dynamic model of",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779968261719,
        667.3972778320312,
        563.035400390625,
        676.3038330078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the robot or its surroundings a priori. The ﬁrst component is",
      "bbox": [
        311.9779968261719,
        679.353271484375,
        563.0320434570312,
        688.2598266601562
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "an environment model, learned online. To ﬁnd high reward ac-",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        691.3082885742188,
        563.0355834960938,
        700.21484375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "tions (i.e., motion plans) for this model, the second component",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        703.2633056640625,
        563.0357055664062,
        712.1698608398438
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "is an RL agent. Since the agent may create unsafe plans, our",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        715.21826171875,
        563.03564453125,
        724.1248168945312
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "third component is a safety layer that combines data-driven",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        727.1732788085938,
        563.0355224609375,
        736.079833984375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "reachability analysis with differentiable collision checking to",
      "bbox": [
        311.97802734375,
        739.1282958984375,
        563.0354614257812,
        748.0348510742188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    }
